  "salt": "XM9HC7Mn6lDzQOH4alO5wA==",
  "text": "Fairy music is a folkloric motif. The fairy folk loved music and were tireless admirers of a good tune. They took a fine piper or harper to play at their dances, then sent the musician home. The pay was often a haunting tune with a planxty, a hypnotic break in rhythm that marks fairy music. The harper Turlough O'Carolan slept on a fairy rath and woke filled with wild music. Fairy music heard from midnight to dawn came from fairy mounds or from all around an unseen place. A dim patch on a bog could give way into Fairyland. The music was never somber. It made the body dance. Endless dance in Fairyland let years slip by, while on earth a cursed dancer died from the strain.",
